\textbf{The verdict:} Multiple lines of evidence consistently show no overfitting. The model's performance on new data matches training data, coefficients are stable, and we have far more events than predictors. If anything, we erred on the side of caution, potentially leaving performance on the table to ensure generalizability.

\textbf{Why this matters:} Overfit models fail in practice—they capture noise rather than signal. Our extensive validation means veterinary authorities can trust these predictions for real-world surveillance decisions.''
