\textbf{Analysis:}
\begin{itemize}
    \item RF/GBM gain 0.006-0.008 AUC (0.6-0.8\% improvement)
    \item Difference is not statistically significant (overlapping CIs)
    \item Improvement is operationally negligible (78\% vs 79\% correct)
    \item For disease surveillance, this doesn't change decisions
\end{itemize}

\textbf{3. Sample Size and Complexity:}
\begin{itemize}
    \item With 1,976 events and 12 predictors, we have ample data
    \item ML methods excel with: high dimensionality, complex interactions, weak signals
    \item Our setting: moderate dimensions, clear main effects, strong signals
    \item Logistic regression is appropriate and sufficient
    \item Occam's Razor: simpler model preferred when performance is equivalent
